<actions>
<action id="A">
<title>Architectural Ingestion</title>
<description>(SDD+TDAD Baseline)</description>
<instructions>
1. Read `specs/constitution.md` for global platform invariants.
2. Identify the active feature directory (e.g., `specs/001-cloudnexus-platform-architecture/002-resource-monitoring-aws-health/`).
3. Read the relevant `prd.md`, `spec.md`, and `data-model.md` to establish the "Design Intent."
</instructions>
</action>

<action id="B">
<title>Git Context</title>
<instructions>
1. Run: `git merge-base main HEAD` to find the common ancestor commit
2. Run: `git diff --name-only $(git merge-base main HEAD) HEAD` to list all files changed in this branch
3. **Filter out test files**: Exclude files matching test patterns using grep -v:
   ```bash
   git diff --name-only $(git merge-base main HEAD) HEAD | grep -v -E '(_test_|\.test\.|\.spec\.|_spec_|[/-]test[/-]|[/-]tests[/-]|[/-]spec[/-])'
   ```
4. This defines the **complete walkthrough scope** - only changes introduced by this branch
</instructions>
<insight>
We use merge-base (not `git diff main HEAD`) because:
- Main may have new commits since this branch was created
- We want to review ONLY what this branch adds, not external changes
- This gives a clean "before/after" view of the branch's impact
</insight>
</action>

